## Static apt configuration for the build image. NOT generated at image-build time.
##
## Pinned to the same snapshot.debian.org timestamp the build uses under
## '--freshness frozen', so the tools installed here and the packages the build
## resolves come from one snapshot. The base image digest is pinned; without this
## the packages layered on top were not, and a DSA moving a runtime library ahead
## of the snapshot makes a '-dev' package from the snapshot, carrying a strict '='
## dependency on it, uninstallable.
##
## Both archives take the same timestamp: snapshot.debian.org resolves a pin per
## archive independently, to the nearest preceding snapshot.
##
## https, not http: apt's integrity guarantee is the 'Signed-By' keyring, but the
## transport is not a place to give ground. dm-update-frozen-snapshot queries this
## host over https through scurl for the same reason.
##
## dm-update-frozen-snapshot rewrites the timestamp here together with
## build_sources/debian_stable_frozen_clearnet.sources and
## build_sources/frozen-snapshot-timestamp, and refuses if the three disagree.
## Keep timestamp-shaped strings out of these comments: the pin is read from the
## 'URIs:' lines, and an example date in a comment is exactly the ambiguity that
## costs an afternoon.
Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20260730T083809Z
Suites: trixie trixie-updates
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Enabled: yes
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg

Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/20260730T083809Z
Suites: trixie-security
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Enabled: yes
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg
